desc(
	mode: "source",
	language: "general",
	title: "Var In Href",
	title_zh: "检测到Var In Href",
	type: vuln,
	level: middle,
	rule_id: "source-insecure-api-var-in-href",
	risk: "Security",
	desc: <<<DESC
Migrated from Semgrep rule `var-in-href` (/tmp/semgrep-rules/javascript/express/security/audit/xss/ejs/var-in-href.yaml).
Original message: Detected a template variable used in an anchor tag with the 'href' attribute. This allows a malicious actor to input the 'javascript:' URI and is subject to cross- site scripting (XSS) attacks. If using a relative URL, start with a literal forward slash and concatenate the URL, like this: href='/<%= link %>'. You may also consider setting the Content Security Policy (CSP) header.

CWE: CWE-79: Improper Neutralization of Input During Web Page Generation ('Cross-site Scripting')
References:
- https://flask.palletsprojects.com/en/1.1.x/security/#cross-site-scripting-xss#:~:text=javascript:%20URI
- https://github.com/pugjs/pug/issues/2952
DESC,
	solution: <<<SOLUTION
Review the flagged code and follow the framework's secure coding guidance: use safe APIs, escape output, and avoid hardcoded credentials.
SOLUTION,
	alert_min: 1,
	"file://pos.ejs": <<<POS
<a"sy[0 utL&88 ""Q<href
		
=YJM(8q<%%>6;[>

POS,
	"safefile://neg.sample": <<<NEG
# safe sample
no secrets here
just regular code
NEG,
)

${*.ejs}.pattern_regex(/<a.*href\s*=[^>]*?[^\/&=]<%.*?%>.*?>/) as $p0
${*.html}.pattern_regex(/<a.*href\s*=[^>]*?[^\/&=]<%.*?%>.*?>/) as $p1
$p0 + $p1 as $hit
alert $hit for {
	level: "middle",
	title: "Var In Href",
	title_zh: "检测到Var In Href",
	message: "Var In Href",
}
